  "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image displays a hand with a finger pointing upward, overlaid with text claiming 'only 1.4% of white people ever owned slaves' and concluding 'so blaming the entire white race is racism at it's finest!'. The overall intent is to dismiss or invalidate the concept of systemic racism by arguing that since only a small percentage of white people owned slaves, blaming the entire white race is inherently racist. This is a hateful message because it targets an entire racial group based on historical actions of a minority within that group, using a false equivalence to justify racial blame-shifting. The visual of the finger pointing up is often used to signify 'I'm right' or 'you're wrong', reinforcing the confrontational and accusatory tone. The meme attempts to delegitimize racial discourse by conflating individual historical behavior with collective racial identity, which is a form of racialized hate speech that ignores the structural and systemic nature of racism.",
